    <!-- Clamp-down notice (issue #298, generalising issue #84's one-off 60 -> 45 migration): shown
         whenever the stored retention window no longer fits this device's *current*
         DeviceMemoryBudget-derived ceiling (a heavier release, less free memory right now, or a
         downgrade). Never shown to a user already at or below the current ceiling. -->
    <string name="settings_retention_clamp_notice_title">Retention window reduced</string>
    <!-- Not a plural, same reasoning as settings_retention_value_active_cd above: %1$d is the raw
         previously-stored value and %2$d is this device's current computed ceiling, both
         multiples of 5, so neither is ever 1. -->
    <string name="settings_retention_clamp_notice_body" tools:ignore="PluralsCandidate">Your retention window was reduced from %1$d to %2$d minutes because it no longer fits on this device.</string>
    <string name="settings_retention_clamp_notice_dismiss">Got it</string>

    <!-- Resize-refused notice (issue #272): shown when a live settings change was refused because
         resizing the audio buffer while capture is running would not fit in this device's current
         heap. The previous, still-active setting stays in force, a refusal, never a crash and
         never a silent no-op. Not a plural: the stepper only ever lands on multiples of 5, at
         least 5 (see settings_retention_value_active_cd above), so %1$d is never 1; %2$d is a
         computed byte count that also never lands on exactly 1 MB. -->
    <string name="settings_resize_error_title">Setting not applied</string>
